# .npmignore — M035 P02 T05 bundle-hygiene contract.
#
# Notes on layered filtering:
#   - package.json `files:` is the primary whitelist (selects whole
#     top-level subtrees: bin/, commands/, scripts/, templates/,
#     references/, packaging/install/, packaging/bundle/,
#     packaging/npm/, etc.).
#   - When `files:` is present, the ROOT .npmignore is largely
#     subordinate to the whitelist for top-level entries — but per-
#     subdirectory .npmignore files (e.g. scripts/verify/.npmignore,
#     templates/conversus-presets/.npmignore) DO prune dogfood-only
#     artifacts from inside whitelisted subtrees. That is where the
#     M035 P02 T05 bundle-hygiene rule-1 enforcement actually lives.
#   - This root file is a defense-in-depth backstop and a discoverable
#     pointer for future maintainers.
#
# See .orchestrator/proposals/m035-bundle-hygiene-pre-publish-filter.md
# and tools/verify/m035-p02-npm-pack-contents.sh for the contract.
# See packaging/bundle/build-bundle.sh apply_bundle_hygiene_filter for
# the build-time mirror of the same two rules.

# Defense-in-depth: dirs that should never appear in the tarball.
.orchestrator/
specs/
tests/
tools/
docs/
wiki/
.github/
.planning/
.git/
node_modules/

# Defense-in-depth: dogfood-only milestone-internal verifiers (real
# enforcement is per-subdir .npmignore files; this is a backstop).
scripts/verify/m[0-9]*-p[0-9]*-*
tools/verify/m[0-9]*-p[0-9]*-*
templates/conversus-presets/m[0-9]*-p[0-9]*-*

# Editor/scratch debris.
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.tmp
*~
